{"id":"h06t4","name":"Versioned Config Store","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["queries"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Implement a small configuration store used by our services. Each query is a list of strings; process them in order and return one string per query.</p>\n<p>The store holds keys per service. Each service has its own <b>version</b> counter, starting at 0. Every query that really changes a service increases its version by 1 and records the new state of the service as that version.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>[\"SET\", service, key, value]</code>: sets the key. Returns the new version of the service. If the key already has exactly this value, nothing changes and the current version is returned.</li>\n<li><code>[\"DELETE\", service, key]</code>: removes the key. Returns the new version, or <code>\"missing\"</code> if the key does not exist (nothing changes).</li>\n<li><code>[\"GET\", service, key]</code>: returns the current value, or <code>\"\"</code> if there is none.</li>\n<li><code>[\"GET_AT\", service, key, version]</code>: returns the value the key had at that version of the service (version 0 is the empty service), or <code>\"\"</code>. If the version is greater than the current version, returns <code>\"invalid\"</code>.</li>\n<li><code>[\"ROLLBACK\", service, version]</code>: makes the state of the service equal to its state at that version. This is a change: it creates a new version, which is returned. Returns <code>\"invalid\"</code> if the version is greater than the current version. Rolling back to a state equal to the current one still creates a new version.</li>\n<li><code>[\"SCAN\", service, prefix]</code>: returns the current keys that start with <code>prefix</code>, as <code>\"key=value\"</code> items sorted by key and joined with <code>\",\"</code>, or <code>\"\"</code>.</li>\n<li><code>[\"CHANGED\", service, v1, v2]</code>: returns the keys whose value differs between versions <code>v1</code> and <code>v2</code> (a key present in only one of them differs), sorted and joined with <code>\",\"</code>, or <code>\"\"</code>. Returns <code>\"invalid\"</code> if one of the versions is greater than the current version.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Versions in queries are written as strings of digits. An unknown service is an empty service at version 0.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>queries = [[\"SET\", \"api\", \"timeout\", \"30\"], [\"SET\", \"api\", \"retries\", \"3\"], [\"SET\", \"api\", \"timeout\", \"30\"], [\"SET\", \"api\", \"timeout\", \"45\"], [\"GET_AT\", \"api\", \"timeout\", \"1\"], [\"DELETE\", \"api\", \"retries\"], [\"DELETE\", \"api\", \"retries\"], [\"ROLLBACK\", \"api\", \"2\"], [\"GET\", \"api\", \"retries\"], [\"SCAN\", \"api\", \"t\"], [\"CHANGED\", \"api\", \"3\", \"5\"], [\"GET_AT\", \"api\", \"timeout\", \"9\"], [\"GET\", \"web\", \"x\"]]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"1\", \"2\", \"2\", \"3\", \"30\", \"4\", \"missing\", \"5\", \"3\", \"timeout=30\", \"timeout\", \"invalid\", \"\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.array.string queries<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(queries):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["système à plusieurs commandes","versions","retour arrière","tri de sortie","cas limites"],"minutes":35,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solution(queries)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Ici, la valeur attendue est une liste : compare ce que tu renvoies à « Expected return value » dans les résultats.</li><li>La comparaison est exacte (même type, mêmes valeurs, même ordre dans une liste), sauf les nombres décimaux, comparés à 0,000001 près.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 9 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"queries":[["SET","api","timeout","30"],["SET","api","retries","3"],["SET","api","timeout","30"],["SET","api","timeout","45"],["GET_AT","api","timeout","1"],["DELETE","api","retries"],["DELETE","api","retries"],["ROLLBACK","api","2"],["GET","api","retries"],["SCAN","api","t"],["CHANGED","api","3","5"],["GET_AT","api","timeout","9"],["GET","web","x"]]},"expected":{"value":["1","2","2","3","30","4","missing","5","3","timeout=30","timeout","invalid",""]}},{"input":{"queries":[["SET","s","a.b","1"],["SET","s","a.c","2"],["SET","s","b","3"],["SCAN","s","a."],["ROLLBACK","s","0"],["SCAN","s",""],["CHANGED","s","0","4"],["CHANGED","s","3","2"],["ROLLBACK","s","7"],["GET_AT","s","b","4"]]},"expected":{"value":["1","2","3","a.b=1,a.c=2","4","","","b","invalid",""]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}